PKG=a4kt71030
NAME=a4kt710-k30 1.0.0-6 - A4000T onboard SCSI (NCR 53C710) module (root class), k30 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.0-6
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-a4kt71030-1.0.0-6
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 sec 1, C4-2): a role=module entry of the
# #ext kpkg block (line=k30, kabi=k30.1.2), class root, never an ordinary
# entry.  Catalog name a4kt710-k30, pkginst a4kt71030; VERSION is the
# module's own release (kernel/drivers/a4091/module/a4kt710/VERSION), the same on both
# lines.
# 1.0.0-6 carries module 1.0.0-3 (no U77 probe, no dma_off knob, no
# last-command globals), built with gcc-cross-amix 33ebadc (cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc).
APKG_DESC=A4000T onboard SCSI (NCR 53C710) as a root-class kernel module for the 68030 root-class module kernel kernel-k30-m (kabi k30.1.2): /etc/conf/mod.d/a4kt710. Gated on the Kickstart's NCR scsi.device tag; param declared=0 in modreg.local.d disables it. DMA through the core's 030 provider. Needs kernel-k30-m -68 or later (cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc).
DESC=The A4000T's onboard NCR 53C710, the a4091 driver built as its second target, as an amix-dlm kernel module for the 68030 line (kabi k30.1.2): root class, match mobo:a4000t-710, one controller at 0xDD0000 registered with sd at rank mobo (after z3660 and zorro, before ide); polled, never unloaded.  The gate (amix-dlm C4-2 v6 sec 8.1): nothing under 0xDD0000 is touched unless the running Kickstart has the A4000T's cold-start NCR scsi.device ROM tag, the chipset is AGA and a read-only probe of the chip answers; otherwise the load returns ENXIO, silent.  Parameter declared (int, default -1): -1 the tag decides, 0 never touch the window, 1 touch it without the tag.  The package sets no parameter: param declared=0 in /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/a4kt710 disables the controller.  DMA through the core's DDI 1.2 (C4-5), on k30 the core's 030 provider (a bounce pool below 0x08000000): needs kernel-k30-m -68 or later, whose pin is the module's cc=gcc-2.7.2.3-33ebadc, and boot2 at amix-dlm 4003c9f or later.  No major and no device nodes of its own: sd owns the disk majors and nodes.  /etc/conf/modreg.d/a4kt710 holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  MIT.
